 true] [17592186343811 1113 #uuid "67dbd2c9-c2b1-519d-a98b-db897636de6f" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343811 1145 "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the products of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$  is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle because $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not one of the known solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343813 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343814 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343815 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343816 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343817 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1041 "selection" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343817 13194139535326 true] [17592186343812 1110 #uuid "d27e28cc-8bfa-530d-8835-f467eec06e85" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343813 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535326 true] [17592186343813 1111 #uuid "c12f1c6a-7897-5050-955e-c30d6cb6868e" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343814 1034 "I only" 13194139535326 true] [17592186343814 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535326 t